+add('major','unsupported','224-253; 267-270',
+    'The specified coefficients suffice for reproducible inverse reconstruction, Momocs matching and automatic harmonic selection.',
+    'The inverse, constant terms, phase origin, evaluation positions and reconstruction error metric are absent. Landmark-centering does not force the arc-length mean to zero. Momocs starts its first segment at the last vertex, whereas the spec anchors index 1 at T. The denominator for the 99 percent power rule and the zero-higher-power case are also undefined.',
+    'The text gives only n=1..H equations and asks for an inverse within a stated tolerance without stating one. Installed efourier.default uses Dx <- coo[,1] - coo[,1][c(nr,1:(nr-1))]. A centered triangle has nonzero Fourier DC (0.0274850704906, 0.0393039712659), recorded in checks.log.',
+    'Specify x(t)=x0+sum(a_n cos+b_n sin), the analogous y(t), the arc-length constant terms or an explicit recentering convention, t=0 and polygon closure. Reconcile the Momocs fixture phase explicitly. Define evaluation times, error units/tolerance and which original/aligned outline is overlaid. Select H against a fixed declared reference spectrum and handle zero residual power.',
+    'An asymmetric polygon passes coefficient matching after the documented phase conversion and reconstructs in the declared frame. A circle, a sharp polygon, H below 16, and a zero-residual-power spectrum have deterministic results.')
