+add('major','unsupported','119-121; 179-190; 347-350',
+    'Maximum width has a defined longitudinal position, and calibration can be applied to all images after independent downscaling.',
+    'The transverse bounding extent can use extrema at different heights, so it has no unique position along length. Rectangles also have tied maximum-width positions. A shared millimetres-per-downscaled-pixel factor is wrong when images have different resize factors. Full-resolution outline is ambiguous after mandatory downscaling.',
+    'Width is defined as extent perpendicular to u, followed by position of maximum width. All coordinates are declared downscaled in 6.1, while 6.4 requests a full-resolution outline and a checkbox applying current calibration to all images.',
